#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078202 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078558 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01f44f8b-5db2-567a-89ce-9283f2f1b0c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of a Geometric Sequence Given the First Term and Common Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "f6a49cd7-9558-524c-b511-b13bd792cfc5" :question/math-academy-id "e-1509" :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $2$, and the common ratio is $3.$ What is the $9$th term?" :question/worked-solution "The first term is $a_1=2,$ and the common ratio is $r=3,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $9$th term, we can use this formula with $n={\\color{blue}9}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{9} & =2\\cdot {3}^{9-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{8} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6561 \\\\  & =13\\,122\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $9$th term is $a_{9}=13\\,122.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078203 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078560 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d82eb202-fec9-5769-a006-67d42b932303" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of a Geometric Sequence Given a Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "f7b26998-6137-54f9-bfe1-a2c3ba5eb0f9" :question/math-academy-id "e-1510" :question/problem "Given that the $5$th term of a geometric sequence is $9$, and the common ratio is $3,$ find the second term." :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=3,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1.$ We know that the $5$th term is $a_5=9,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{5-1} \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{4} \\\\ 9 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot 81 \\\\ \\frac{9}{81} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is $a_1=\\dfrac{1}{9},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{n-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {3}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can use this formula to compute the second term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot {3}^{2-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second term is $a_2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078204 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078559 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5760a53a-1a0c-568e-ac9c-c820eaad3010" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Formula for the Nth Term of a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "4bf89b8f-f713-51b5-8536-5aa5b08f16d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-1511" :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of a sequence if the $6$th term is $80$ and the common ratio is $-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=-2,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term $a_1.$ We know that the $6$th term is $a_6=80,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{6-1} \\\\ 80 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{5} \\\\ 80 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-32) \\\\ -\\frac{80}{32} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is $a_1=-\\dfrac{5}{2},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify a bit further by manipulating the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{5}{2}(-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-2)^{-1}\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-2)^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078560 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d82eb202-fec9-5769-a006-67d42b932303" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of a Geometric Sequence Given a Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a702943-5d20-5d78-b4eb-5b9620b8469b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{5}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549330} {:answer/id #uuid "1d9acfbd-b37d-5bf8-8563-021375b3f0ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-(-5)^{n-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549375} {:answer/id #uuid "71563d96-72fd-5a7a-873a-b97ad8340ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549530} {:answer/id #uuid "eec28517-10af-546d-b87d-a5fb95584b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549756} {:answer/id #uuid "fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{5}^{n-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fce13607-7057-5951-b22c-0a53487566f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-{5}^{n-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549791} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d82d16e-44b2-54a6-8e45-2ab848923d07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5f78cff-3c2d-5ff5-b715-c8fb25e53460" :question/math-academy-id "q-109828" :question/problem "Given that the $5$th term of a geometric sequence is $-125$, and the common ratio is $5,$ find the formula for the $n$th term." :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=5,$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $5$th term is ${a}_{5}=-125,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{5-1} \\\\ -125 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4} \\\\ -{5}^{3} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{5},$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {5}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {5}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{5}^{n-1}}{5} \\\\  & =-{5}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549981 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078558 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01f44f8b-5db2-567a-89ce-9283f2f1b0c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of a Geometric Sequence Given the First Term and Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "910334bb-a236-530a-b15b-4e9e5b6ad92e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549599} :answer-field/id #uuid "b77092c7-1268-5f33-a5db-81532ae19c78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91775cc6-b3ff-5403-8a6d-5a5294e1af4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-265737" :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $-\\frac{1}{81},$ and the common ratio is $-3.$ The $9$th term of this sequence is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The first term is ${a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{81},$ and the common ratio is $r=-3,$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $9$th term, we can use this formula with $n=9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{9} & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{9-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{81}\\cdot (-3)^{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{3}^{4}}\\cdot {3}^{8} \\\\  & =-{3}^{4} \\\\  & =-81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $9$th term is ${a}_{9}=-81.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078558 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01f44f8b-5db2-567a-89ce-9283f2f1b0c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of a Geometric Sequence Given the First Term and Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dd5ec84-7a08-5f98-8682-c2c50317fdda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549376} :answer-field/id #uuid "26653816-dfb8-59e5-8d87-31577cdbb120" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f438fee9-fd2e-5bc4-8ed6-aceb6e4fcc33" :question/math-academy-id "q-265738" :question/problem "The first term of a geometric sequence is $32,$ and the common ratio is $-\\frac{1}{2}.$  The $12$th term of this sequence is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The first term is ${a}_{1}=32,$ and the common ratio is $r=-\\frac{1}{2},$ so we can write the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the $12$th term, we can use this formula with $n=12:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\ {a}_{12} & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{12-1} \\\\  & =32\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{11} \\\\  & =-{2}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{2}^{11}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{2}^{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $12$th term is ${a}_{12}=-\\frac{1}{64}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078560 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d82eb202-fec9-5769-a006-67d42b932303" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of a Geometric Sequence Given a Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7fc47b7-94cb-597e-9fb8-34e73e5166b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549781} :answer-field/id #uuid "821f6ff9-8b02-5321-9f6c-8231f646103b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb4d13f6-05f0-58f1-8216-e5e0e82521cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-265843" :question/problem "If the sixth term of a geometric sequence is $\\frac{1}{16}$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{1}{4},$ then the third term of this sequence is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=\\frac{1}{4},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $6$th term is ${a}_{6}=16,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{6-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{16} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{4}^{2}} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{4}^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{{4}^{5}}{{4}^{2}} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=64,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can use this formula to compute the third term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =64\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3-1} \\\\  & ={4}^{3}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & ={4}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third term  is ${a}_{3}=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078559 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5760a53a-1a0c-568e-ac9c-c820eaad3010" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Formula for the Nth Term of a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa368f5-9980-5af5-a908-3b9b819b0121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=100\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549331} {:answer/id #uuid "a7cb3144-a22f-5f9b-a7a4-6681a52052c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=16\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549632} {:answer/id #uuid "a8bc2a3c-15ca-50bd-b78f-91ffcfb5a2d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=49\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549635} {:answer/id #uuid "cc516a3f-e478-5de4-865d-84d26bdbc656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=64\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549700} {:answer/id #uuid "eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=81\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eca10867-76a4-52f1-be58-955b24419718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=81\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549752} :answer-field/id #uuid "93f0a508-6eba-52dd-97c6-cb5ace58658c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1bbae00a-a76f-5b1d-a767-0acf7498bde8" :question/math-academy-id "q-5449" :question/problem "Find the equation for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence if the $5$th term is $16$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=\\frac{2}{3},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $5$th term is ${a}_{5}=16,$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{5-1} \\\\ 16 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4} \\\\ {2}^{4} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot (\\frac{{2}^{4}}{{3}^{4}}) \\\\ \\frac{{2}^{4}\\cdot {3}^{4}}{{2}^{4}} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {3}^{4} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ 81 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=81,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =81\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078559 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5760a53a-1a0c-568e-ac9c-c820eaad3010" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Formula for the Nth Term of a Geometric Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b365dcf-dfb8-5ede-acf7-bff7804315f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=125\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549334} {:answer/id #uuid "7d26afe6-a3f8-5d84-83c8-1468c5a521e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-125\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549550} {:answer/id #uuid "838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549561} {:answer/id #uuid "d08576a1-0a16-5570-9a0f-9b630cd00e74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-625\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549704} {:answer/id #uuid "f723a1bb-4bd1-5093-8a09-931299bce976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "838f58f2-22d1-5628-b984-cb6bd81d4f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549561} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6e6324-1bb7-5c0e-a897-1048511dc113" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18bc1e21-0c4b-52f3-824f-e719cd86e034" :question/math-academy-id "q-5450" :question/problem "Find the equation for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence if the $6$th term is $-\\frac{1}{5}$ and the common ratio is $-\\frac{1}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "The common ratio is $r=-\\frac{1}{5},$ so we can start writing the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we still need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}.$ We know that the $6$th term is ${a}_{6}=-\\frac{1}{5},$ so we can solve for the first term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{6-1} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & =-{a}_{1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & =-{a}_{1}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{{5}^{5}}) \\\\ {5}^{4} & ={a}_{1} \\\\ 625 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the first term is ${a}_{1}=625,$ we can complete the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =625\\cdot {(-\\frac{1}{5})}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
